WEBVTT

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:04.598
Just a minute.

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.798
I'll... I'll,
I'll be right there.

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:16.746
I'm coming. I'm coming.

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.183
Deanna!

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:25.554
Hello, Reg.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.684
I'm so glad you could make it.

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:29.058
It's wonderful to see you.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:32.627
Would it be all right
if I came inside?

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:33.723
Yeah. Of course.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:34.892
Of course!

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.333
Come in, come in.

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:39.167
Is-is there something
I can get you?

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:42.299
Some, um, some coffee? Tea?

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.637
Oh, wait a minute.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.905
Don't... don't tell me.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:47.241
Chocolate ice cream.

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.644
You know me too well.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:50.148
But just one scoop.

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:51.808
I'm watching my figure.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:52.977
Why?!

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.987
You... you look lovely.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:57.580
You always knew
how to flatter me.

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:01.656
Would you like me to get it?

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.696
Get... get what?

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:04.923
The ice cream.

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:06.625
Right! Right!
The ice cream.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:07.927
No, no. No, no, no.

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:09.468
Come in, come in.

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:10.662
Sit down...

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:12.364
make yourself comfortable.

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.204
It's a nice place.

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.335
Thanks.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:21.073
One scoop
of chocolate ice cream.

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:22.614
Did you just move in?

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:23.614
No, no.

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:25.310
I've been here, uh...

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:26.852
almost two years.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.650
I just haven't
had a chance to unpack.

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:33.952
Is everything all right, Reg?

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:34.959
Of course.

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:36.528
Why, why wouldn't it be?

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:39.429
To be honest,
you seem a little on edge.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:42.400
Do I? Oh, oh,
it's just that I'm...

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:43.834
I'm excited to see you.

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:45.700
I'm excited to see you, too.

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:46.739
I think Geordi's

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:48.398
a little disappointed

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:51.069
I didn't invite
him to come along.

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:53.135
Yes, I... well,
I-I was hoping to get...

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:54.646
get together with him, too,

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:57.308
uh, before
the Enterprise leaves orbit,

00:01:57.383 --> 00:02:00.181
but I just wanted to spend
some time with you first.

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:01.220
That's all right,

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.016
- isn't it?
- Of course it is.

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:10.920
I hear you've been working
on the Pathfinder Project.

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:12.521
Well, I...

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:14.897
I was, uh...

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.435
I'm not anymore.

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:17.435
What happened?

00:02:17.504 --> 00:02:18.436
Oh, uh...

00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:20.234
nothing... really.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:23.469
Just got to be a lot of, uh...

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.033
pressure.

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:26.100
Well, hello!

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:27.908
Neelix!

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:29.881
Oh, he's not used to company.
Oh.

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:32.747
It's not polite
to eat our guest's food.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:34.878
If you're hungry,
just say so.

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:37.787
Deanna, uh, Neelix.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.415
Neelix?

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.460
That's an unusual name.

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:45.391
Maybe we should introduce him

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:46.932
to Data's cat, Spot.

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.964
I have a feeling

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:54.473
you didn't ask me here
to reminisce.

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:56.873
Tell me what's wrong.

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:05.642
I've lost myself, Deanna.

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:07.948
Lost yourself?

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.490
In Voyager.

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:13.458
I've become obsessed

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:16.427
with Voyager.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.233
Here you are on shore leave

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:09.366
and what do I do?

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:12.468
I lure you into
a counseling session.

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:13.739
Don't worry about that.

00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:15.576
The important thing is

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:18.310
I'm here now,
and I want to help.

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:19.749
Thank you.

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:21.150
Now...

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.279
start at the beginning.

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:25.517
Has it ever occurred to you

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:27.559
that a tachyon beam

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:30.323
directed at a class-B
itinerant pulsar

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:32.694
could produce
enough gravimetric energy

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:34.733
to create an artificial
singularity?

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:36.428
I can't say it has.

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.026
It occurred to me,

00:05:38.104 --> 00:05:42.541
but my supervisors thought
it was an abuse of MIDAS.

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:44.132
MIDAS?

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:45.541
The, uh, Mutara Interdimensional

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:47.545
Deep Space Transponder Array.

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:49.376
Reg, you're losing me.

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:50.677
I'm sorry.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.615
The beginning.

00:05:52.685 --> 00:05:55.313
The beginning... right.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:06:01.656
Well, I suppose it all started
in the holodeck.

00:06:01.728 --> 00:06:03.252
Doesn't it always?

00:06:04.297 --> 00:06:05.491
Go on.

00:06:05.565 --> 00:06:07.192
Well...

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:09.166
I...

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:11.499
I was running
a few simulations.

00:06:11.571 --> 00:06:14.404
Computer, boost the gain
on Voyager's transceiver

00:06:14.474 --> 00:06:15.668
by 20 percent.

00:06:15.742 --> 00:06:18.006
Transceiver gain is at maximum.

00:06:19.512 --> 00:06:22.447
Apply a narrowband filter
to the signal processor.

00:06:22.515 --> 00:06:24.380
Filter engaged.

00:06:25.985 --> 00:06:27.748
Voyager, come in.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.014
Come in, Voyager.

00:06:30.056 --> 00:06:31.785
Voyager, come in.

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:33.849
This is Starfleet Command.

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:36.053
Voyager, come in, Voyager.

00:06:36.129 --> 00:06:38.188
Good. Good, good.

00:06:38.264 --> 00:06:41.062
Now, lower the filter band
by.3 kilohertz.

00:06:41.134 --> 00:06:43.432
Reg, what are you doing?

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:44.936
Oh.

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:46.938
Uh, um, Pete.

00:06:47.073 --> 00:06:49.234
I-I-I was just, uh...

00:06:49.308 --> 00:06:50.935
Yes, running
another simulation.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.102
I can see that.

00:06:52.178 --> 00:06:53.611
What about
the transmitter diagnostics?

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:55.670
Right. The diagnostics.

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:57.943
You have finished them,
haven't you?

00:06:58.017 --> 00:06:59.075
Uh... almost.

00:06:59.152 --> 00:07:00.744
Almost isn't good enough.

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:04.187
We've got Admiral Paris
first thing in the morning.

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:05.349
Admiral Paris?

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:07.017
Don't tell me you forgot.

00:07:07.093 --> 00:07:08.993
Oh, no, of-of... of course not.

00:07:09.061 --> 00:07:10.892
I-I-I just got
the days mixed up.

00:07:10.997 --> 00:07:12.294
Reg!

00:07:12.365 --> 00:07:13.696
Computer, end program.

00:07:13.766 --> 00:07:16.894
Now that I think about it,
it's a good thing

00:07:17.036 --> 00:07:19.869
that Admiral Paris
is coming tomorrow.

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:21.133
We can brief the Admiral

00:07:21.207 --> 00:07:22.196
on my theory.

00:07:22.275 --> 00:07:23.401
What theory?

00:07:23.476 --> 00:07:24.534
I've been going over

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.578
the interstellar
phenomena forecasts

00:07:26.646 --> 00:07:27.908
from Deep Space 9.

00:07:28.014 --> 00:07:29.379
They are predicting, uh,

00:07:29.449 --> 00:07:31.713
a class-B itinerant pulsar

00:07:31.784 --> 00:07:34.753
will pass within
four billion kilometers

00:07:34.821 --> 00:07:36.812
of the MIDAS Array
in three days.

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:38.880
You think the pulsar
might damage the Array?

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.619
No, no. The
shields will hold.

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:41.887
Actually, I was thinking, uh,

00:07:41.961 --> 00:07:44.156
we could use the pulsar
to our own advantage.

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:45.822
How?

00:07:45.898 --> 00:07:48.560
Suppose... suppose we instructed
the Array to direct

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:50.397
a tachyon beam at the pulsar.

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:53.906
Theoretically, we could
produce a gravimetric surge

00:07:53.973 --> 00:07:57.670
powerful enough to create
an artificial wormhole.

00:07:57.743 --> 00:08:01.110
We could establish
two-way communication

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:02.442
with Voyager.

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:03.880
Reg, you're dreaming again.

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:06.484
No, no, I-I really think
this could work.

00:08:06.552 --> 00:08:07.712
Based on
my simulations, that...

00:08:07.787 --> 00:08:09.778
Based on your last series
of simulations,

00:08:09.856 --> 00:08:11.790
we wasted six months
trying to develop

00:08:11.858 --> 00:08:12.847
that transwarp probe.

00:08:12.925 --> 00:08:15.052
This... this is
different. This...

00:08:15.127 --> 00:08:17.357
Reg... I really appreciate

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:18.727
your imagination.

00:08:18.798 --> 00:08:21.596
It's what makes you such
a valuable part of this team,

00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:23.567
but I'm not about to tell
the Admiral

00:08:23.636 --> 00:08:26.298
that we've found a way
for him to chat with his son

00:08:26.372 --> 00:08:27.896
because of some
cockeyed theory

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:29.632
that only exists up here.

00:08:29.709 --> 00:08:32.735
Now, please,
finish those diagnostics.

00:08:32.812 --> 00:08:34.302
Yes, sir.

00:08:39.785 --> 00:08:41.013
And, Reg,

00:08:41.087 --> 00:08:42.384
remember...

00:08:42.455 --> 00:08:43.922
while the Admiral's here,

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:45.048
I do the talking.

00:08:45.124 --> 00:08:46.182
You do the talking.

00:08:46.259 --> 00:08:47.783
Understood.

00:08:49.695 --> 00:08:51.595
Pete was only trying
to look out for me,

00:08:51.664 --> 00:08:54.258
but I was sure
my plan would work.

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:56.130
I, I just couldn't give it up.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:07.770
Burning the midnight oil.

00:09:07.847 --> 00:09:10.873
I-I finished, uh,
the diagnostics, sir.

00:09:11.017 --> 00:09:12.609
Yes. I know.

00:09:12.685 --> 00:09:14.175
I looked them over.

00:09:14.253 --> 00:09:15.515
Good job.

00:09:19.959 --> 00:09:23.053
Well, why don't you
call it a day?

00:09:23.129 --> 00:09:26.155
I just, uh, have
a few more things

00:09:26.232 --> 00:09:27.699
to take care of.

00:09:27.767 --> 00:09:29.962
Well, see you tomorrow, then.

00:09:31.771 --> 00:09:35.298
Oh. Reg, why don't, um...

00:09:35.374 --> 00:09:37.171
why don't you drop by tonight

00:09:37.243 --> 00:09:38.835
when you're through here?

00:09:38.911 --> 00:09:40.242
"Drop by"?

00:09:40.313 --> 00:09:41.575
Come to the house.

00:09:41.647 --> 00:09:42.841
Have some coffee.

00:09:42.915 --> 00:09:44.906
Angie's sister
is in from Boston.

00:09:44.984 --> 00:09:46.611
I, uh...

00:09:46.686 --> 00:09:48.278
I think she might like you.

00:09:48.354 --> 00:09:53.121
I-I don't, I don't think I...
can, uh...

00:09:53.192 --> 00:09:56.753
I'm spending the evening
with, um...

00:09:56.829 --> 00:09:58.296
Neelix.

00:09:58.364 --> 00:10:00.389
Correct me if I'm wrong, Reg,

00:10:00.466 --> 00:10:02.434
but Neelix is your cat.

00:10:04.971 --> 00:10:07.940
Well, if you change your mind.

00:10:08.007 --> 00:10:09.565
Thanks.

00:10:09.642 --> 00:10:11.610
I'll... I'll try.

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:15.670
But I couldn't leave,

00:10:15.748 --> 00:10:17.181
not until
I'd strengthened my case

00:10:17.249 --> 00:10:18.511
for accessing the MIDAS Array.

00:10:18.584 --> 00:10:21.644
The meeting with Admiral Paris
was only 14 hours away,

00:10:21.721 --> 00:10:23.712
and I hadn't come up
with anything.

00:10:23.789 --> 00:10:26.257
Poring over the data
wasn't helping.

00:10:26.325 --> 00:10:33.891
I decided that what I needed
was, um, a little inspiration.

00:10:33.966 --> 00:10:35.490
Computer...

00:10:35.568 --> 00:10:38.059
activate hologrid
Mess Hall scenario

00:10:38.137 --> 00:10:40.071
Barclay 11-Gamma.

00:10:45.945 --> 00:10:46.969
Hey, Reg.

00:10:47.113 --> 00:10:48.978
Warning. The
shark is circling.

00:10:50.016 --> 00:10:51.278
Let the games begin.

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:52.442
What'll it be, Reg?

00:10:52.518 --> 00:10:53.678
The usual.

00:10:53.753 --> 00:10:55.880
Computer, one milk, warm.

00:10:55.955 --> 00:10:57.286
Oh, thanks, Harry.

00:10:57.356 --> 00:10:59.722
Just trying to get
on your good side,

00:10:59.792 --> 00:11:01.885
so you'll go easy
on me tonight.

00:11:01.961 --> 00:11:03.724
Ah, you know
what I always say...

00:11:03.796 --> 00:11:05.491
if you can't stand
the heat...

00:11:05.564 --> 00:11:07.191
Get out of the warp core.

00:11:07.266 --> 00:11:08.358
Sit down, Lieutenant,

00:11:08.434 --> 00:11:10.527
and give us mortals
a chance to get even.

00:11:10.603 --> 00:11:11.535
That's an order.

00:11:11.604 --> 00:11:12.764
If you insist, Commander,

00:11:12.838 --> 00:11:14.601
but I think it's only fair
to warn you

00:11:14.674 --> 00:11:15.606
I have no intention

00:11:15.675 --> 00:11:17.802
of letting my winning streak
come to an end.

00:11:19.045 --> 00:11:20.103
Now, where's,

00:11:20.179 --> 00:11:21.646
um, Tuvok?

00:11:21.714 --> 00:11:22.908
He said it's illogical

00:11:22.982 --> 00:11:25.348
to continue losing
to a clearly superior player.

00:11:25.418 --> 00:11:26.885
Oh, that's too bad.

00:11:26.952 --> 00:11:29.352
I love to watch
that Vulcan squirm.

00:11:29.422 --> 00:11:31.447
Now, you all know the rules.

00:11:31.524 --> 00:11:34.118
Deuces, one-eyed jacks
and suicide kings are wild.

00:11:34.193 --> 00:11:37.094
Five of a kind beats
a straight flush every time.

00:11:37.163 --> 00:11:38.391
The man is ruthless.

00:11:38.464 --> 00:11:39.396
He's a killer.

00:11:39.465 --> 00:11:41.194
Now, come on, guys.

00:11:41.267 --> 00:11:43.792
You know it hurts me
to see you lose.

00:11:43.869 --> 00:11:47.600
After all,
you are my best friends.

00:11:49.575 --> 00:11:52.703
I'd hoped that the poker game
would help calm my nerves,

00:11:52.778 --> 00:11:54.643
so that I could get
a decent night's sleep

00:11:54.714 --> 00:11:58.343
before the briefing,
but when I got home that night,

00:11:58.417 --> 00:12:01.352
I couldn't keep my mind
off of Voyager.

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:03.854
I needed to get back
to the holodeck.

00:12:08.494 --> 00:12:10.155
That feels so good.

00:12:10.229 --> 00:12:13.096
Therapeutic massage
can be an effective treatment

00:12:13.165 --> 00:12:14.598
for insomnia, Lieutenant.

00:12:14.667 --> 00:12:17.329
But we need to get to the cause
of your sleeplessness

00:12:17.403 --> 00:12:19.894
if we're going to find
a more permanent solution.

00:12:19.972 --> 00:12:23.169
It's just that every time
I-I close my eyes,

00:12:23.242 --> 00:12:25.073
my mind starts to race.

00:12:25.144 --> 00:12:26.702
Can you be more specific?

00:12:26.779 --> 00:12:28.644
Well, I worry about the project.

00:12:28.714 --> 00:12:31.239
Have I explored the problem
from every angle,

00:12:31.317 --> 00:12:34.150
or is there something else
I should be trying?

00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:35.653
Am I doing enough?

00:12:35.721 --> 00:12:37.518
Hmm.

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:39.080
Acute work-related anxiety.

00:12:39.158 --> 00:12:41.183
Perhaps I should speak
to the Captain

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:42.887
about reducing your schedule.

00:12:42.962 --> 00:12:44.259
Oh, something tells me

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:46.389
she's not going to be able
to help.

00:12:46.465 --> 00:12:48.160
You are an invaluable

00:12:48.234 --> 00:12:51.067
member of this
crew, Mr. Barclay.

00:12:51.137 --> 00:12:52.263
Thank you, Doctor.

00:12:52.338 --> 00:12:54.203
It's nice to be appreciated.

00:12:54.273 --> 00:12:55.399
Hmm.

00:12:56.609 --> 00:12:57.701
Oh!

00:13:00.112 --> 00:13:01.340
Turning in, Reg?

00:13:01.413 --> 00:13:02.573
Yes, sir.

00:13:02.648 --> 00:13:03.808
Hey, Reg.

00:13:03.883 --> 00:13:06.477
For some reason,
I never slept in my apartment

00:13:06.552 --> 00:13:11.387
as comfortably as I did
in my holographic quarters.

00:13:11.457 --> 00:13:15.359
I suppose
I felt more at home on Voyager.

00:13:15.427 --> 00:13:17.395
Mm-hmm.

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:36.410
Good morning, everyone.

00:13:36.482 --> 00:13:37.676
Morning, Reg.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:38.944
You're awfully chipper.

00:13:39.084 --> 00:13:40.449
Ah... slept like a baby.

00:13:40.519 --> 00:13:42.316
Then maybe you've got
the energy to whip up

00:13:42.388 --> 00:13:43.946
one of your famous
cheese omelets.

00:13:44.089 --> 00:13:45.579
Oh, yeah. I'm starved.

00:13:45.658 --> 00:13:48.354
I'm sorry, guys. I have a very
important briefing at 0900.

00:13:48.427 --> 00:13:49.758
Just have time for coffee.

00:13:49.829 --> 00:13:51.490
Uh, don't forget
about tonight.

00:13:51.564 --> 00:13:53.589
Uh... remind me.

00:13:53.666 --> 00:13:54.826
You were supposed to teach me

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:55.958
how to play velocity.

00:13:56.068 --> 00:13:57.228
No. No way.

00:13:57.303 --> 00:13:58.964
Reg and I have
a hoverball game scheduled.

00:13:59.071 --> 00:13:59.969
Don't fight.

00:14:00.072 --> 00:14:01.903
Plenty of me to go around.

00:14:01.974 --> 00:14:05.171
Reg... I'm sorry
to bother you again,

00:14:05.244 --> 00:14:06.302
but I'm
still having trouble

00:14:06.378 --> 00:14:07.675
with the warp core
recalibration.

00:14:07.746 --> 00:14:08.838
It's no problem.

00:14:08.914 --> 00:14:10.404
I'll stop by Engineering later
and talk you through it.

00:14:10.482 --> 00:14:11.414
Thank you.

00:14:11.483 --> 00:14:13.917
I really appreciate it.

00:14:14.019 --> 00:14:17.614
Velocity, hoverball,
warp core recalibrations?

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:20.158
Reg, I don't know
how you do it.

00:14:20.226 --> 00:14:23.218
Let you in on a little secret.

00:14:23.295 --> 00:14:25.126
There's two of me.

00:14:27.833 --> 00:14:32.065
The Delta Quadrant,
Sector 41751, Grid 9.

00:14:32.137 --> 00:14:34.901
Voyager's Doctor reported this
as the ship's position

00:14:34.974 --> 00:14:37.238
when his program was
briefly transferred

00:14:37.309 --> 00:14:39.072
to Starfleet two years ago.

00:14:39.144 --> 00:14:41.112
Assuming they're still
on course for Earth,

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:42.545
we've been able to extrapolate

00:14:42.615 --> 00:14:44.708
a range of likely
trajectories.

00:14:44.783 --> 00:14:47.650
Estimating an average
warp speed of 6.2

00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:50.883
and accounting for various
astronomical obstacles...

00:14:55.527 --> 00:14:57.188
we can reasonably assume
that Voyager

00:14:57.263 --> 00:14:59.424
is now in one of
these three sectors.

00:14:59.498 --> 00:15:01.591
Can we contact them?

00:15:01.667 --> 00:15:03.726
As you know, we've been
working with the Vulcans

00:15:03.802 --> 00:15:05.770
on the deployment
of the MIDAS Array.

00:15:07.806 --> 00:15:10.001
Though we're still
in the testing phase, we think

00:15:10.075 --> 00:15:12.407
it won't be long before we
can use this technology

00:15:12.478 --> 00:15:15.140
to send signals at
hyper-subspace speeds.

00:15:15.214 --> 00:15:18.240
A message that would
normally take years

00:15:18.317 --> 00:15:20.683
to reach its destination
could be received

00:15:20.753 --> 00:15:22.311
by Voyager
in a matter of days.

00:15:22.388 --> 00:15:24.288
Impressive.

00:15:24.356 --> 00:15:26.347
Will they be able to respond?

00:15:26.425 --> 00:15:28.154
No, sir,

00:15:28.227 --> 00:15:30.388
but at least they'll know
we're still looking

00:15:30.462 --> 00:15:31.622
for them.

00:15:31.697 --> 00:15:33.221
We'll send data

00:15:33.299 --> 00:15:34.926
on the hyper-subspace
technology

00:15:35.034 --> 00:15:36.934
and hope they can
eventually use it

00:15:37.002 --> 00:15:38.026
to return the call.

00:15:38.103 --> 00:15:40.162
Excuse me, Admiral Paris.

00:15:40.239 --> 00:15:41.900
Lieutenant Barclay...

00:15:41.974 --> 00:15:43.373
I-I'm sorry, Commander.

00:15:43.442 --> 00:15:45.933
It's just that there may be
a way to establish, uh,

00:15:46.078 --> 00:15:47.841
two-way communication
with Voyager.

00:15:47.913 --> 00:15:49.710
Now is not the time.

00:15:49.782 --> 00:15:52.216
It's all right, Mr. Harkins.

00:15:52.284 --> 00:15:53.911
Let the man speak.

00:15:53.986 --> 00:15:55.613
I'm all ears, son.

00:15:55.688 --> 00:15:57.622
Well, um...

00:15:59.491 --> 00:16:02.358
Well, you see, there's a, uh,

00:16:02.428 --> 00:16:05.625
a class-B
itinerant, uh, pulsar

00:16:05.698 --> 00:16:10.897
uh, and... well-well,
as you probably know, s-sir,

00:16:11.036 --> 00:16:14.199
uh, neutrino emissions, uh...

00:16:14.273 --> 00:16:15.205
oh.

00:16:15.274 --> 00:16:20.109
What I mean to say is

00:16:20.179 --> 00:16:26.209
that with the Array,
we could open an artificial

00:16:26.285 --> 00:16:31.552
uh, uh... a... sing...
a sing, uh, sing-singularity.

00:16:31.623 --> 00:16:32.920
A wormhole?

00:16:33.025 --> 00:16:35.926
Yes! Yes, sir.

00:16:36.061 --> 00:16:40.930
We could use it as a conduit
to-to talk to Voyager.

00:16:41.066 --> 00:16:42.761
I can't give you high marks
for clarity, Lieutenant,

00:16:42.835 --> 00:16:44.496
but you've certainly got
my attention.

00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:46.299
Is there any merit
to what he's saying?

00:16:46.372 --> 00:16:50.274
Mr. Barclay has a tendency
to get ahead of himself, sir.

00:16:50.342 --> 00:16:52.936
Unfortunately,
what he's suggesting

00:16:53.012 --> 00:16:54.479
is beyond our abilities.

00:16:54.546 --> 00:16:56.070
But you haven't even...

00:16:56.148 --> 00:16:56.944
Mr. Barclay!

00:16:57.082 --> 00:16:58.674
I know that I haven't

00:16:58.751 --> 00:17:00.184
explained myself, uh, very well,

00:17:00.252 --> 00:17:01.651
but with all due respect, sir,

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:04.655
what do we have
to lose by trying?

00:17:04.723 --> 00:17:10.787
I think we're forgetting
that there are 150 people

00:17:10.863 --> 00:17:13.798
stranded in the Delta Quadrant.

00:17:13.866 --> 00:17:16.630
I have a son
on that ship, Lieutenant.

00:17:16.702 --> 00:17:20.468
I haven't forgotten that fact
for a single moment.

00:17:20.539 --> 00:17:22.336
I'm sorry, sir.

00:17:22.408 --> 00:17:24.467
I-I didn't, uh...
I didn't mean to...

00:17:24.543 --> 00:17:26.443
Take the rest of
the day off, Reg.

00:17:26.512 --> 00:17:27.536
But...

00:17:27.613 --> 00:17:29.774
That was not a suggestion.

00:17:40.292 --> 00:17:43.887
How did you deal
with your feelings afterwards?

00:17:43.962 --> 00:17:45.224
What do you mean?

00:17:45.297 --> 00:17:48.095
Well... did you talk
to Commander Harkins

00:17:48.167 --> 00:17:50.294
after the meeting...
apologize?

00:17:50.369 --> 00:17:52.633
Well... no.

00:17:52.704 --> 00:17:56.401
I wanted to, uh,
fine tune my plan

00:17:56.475 --> 00:18:00.571
so, I-I just went
right back to work.

00:18:00.646 --> 00:18:02.170
Be more specific.

00:18:02.247 --> 00:18:04.408
What exactly did you do?

00:18:04.483 --> 00:18:05.575
Well, I...

00:18:05.651 --> 00:18:07.881
needed someone to, uh...

00:18:07.986 --> 00:18:09.749
bounce ideas off of,

00:18:09.822 --> 00:18:11.881
someone to help focus
my thoughts.

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:13.252
Sounds reasonable.

00:18:13.325 --> 00:18:15.020
I suppose you... consulted

00:18:15.094 --> 00:18:17.722
with some of your
Pathfinder colleagues.

00:18:17.796 --> 00:18:20.390
Well...

00:18:20.466 --> 00:18:23.333
not exactly.

00:18:23.402 --> 00:18:25.597
You went back to the holodeck,
didn't you?

00:18:25.671 --> 00:18:27.571
They're the only people
that I can talk to.

00:18:27.639 --> 00:18:29.004
They're not people.

00:18:29.074 --> 00:18:31.008
I know...

00:18:31.076 --> 00:18:33.704
but they...
they help me with my work.

00:18:33.779 --> 00:18:37.579
Poker, massages...

00:18:37.649 --> 00:18:39.583
sleeping in
holographic quarters?

00:18:39.651 --> 00:18:41.710
Sounds more like escape
than work.

00:18:41.787 --> 00:18:44.187
I can't concentrate
if I'm not relaxed.

00:18:44.256 --> 00:18:46.224
Can't you relax
with your friends?

00:18:46.291 --> 00:18:47.918
"Friends"?

00:18:47.993 --> 00:18:51.793
Commander Harkins invited you
to his home.

00:18:51.864 --> 00:18:54.856
You went
to the holodeck instead.

00:18:54.933 --> 00:18:57.265
It's not what you're thinking,
Deanna.

00:18:57.336 --> 00:18:59.964
This isn't a relapse
of my holo-addiction.

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:03.073
Okay.

00:19:03.142 --> 00:19:07.374
Tell me how the holograms
helped you with your work.

00:19:07.446 --> 00:19:10.279
Well, I talked to them
about my ideas.

00:19:10.349 --> 00:19:12.783
I worked out
technical problems.

00:19:12.851 --> 00:19:15.217
I need specifics here, people.

00:19:15.287 --> 00:19:17.346
Take us through it again,
Mr. Barclay,

00:19:17.422 --> 00:19:18.480
one step at a time.

00:19:18.557 --> 00:19:20.582
Maybe it'll spark an idea.

00:19:20.659 --> 00:19:22.786
We've got our itinerant pulsar.

00:19:22.861 --> 00:19:26.228
We've got our interdimensional
transponder array.

00:19:26.298 --> 00:19:28.095
How do we get
our wormhole?

00:19:28.167 --> 00:19:30.601
This one could keep
us up all night.

00:19:30.669 --> 00:19:33.832
Oh. We know we can produce
gravimetric energy,

00:19:33.906 --> 00:19:37.103
but... can we do it
at levels high enough

00:19:37.176 --> 00:19:39.235
to create the singularity?

00:19:39.311 --> 00:19:40.403
We're talking

00:19:40.479 --> 00:19:42.572
about a massive
subspace reaction.

00:19:42.648 --> 00:19:45.913
Maybe... that's the problem.

00:19:46.018 --> 00:19:47.610
Reg?

00:19:47.686 --> 00:19:50.120
Maybe we need
to think smaller.

00:19:50.189 --> 00:19:52.123
You're losing me.

00:19:52.191 --> 00:19:55.217
How much bandwidth
do we really need?

00:19:55.294 --> 00:19:57.387
The average wormhole is huge,

00:19:57.462 --> 00:20:00.295
but if we compressed
the datastream...

00:20:00.365 --> 00:20:03.129
We wouldn't need a conduit
anywhere near as big.

00:20:03.202 --> 00:20:04.760
What's your idea?

00:20:06.538 --> 00:20:10.167
A micro-wormhole.

00:20:10.242 --> 00:20:12.210
Impressive.

00:20:12.277 --> 00:20:14.541
You've outdone yourself
this time, Reg.

00:20:14.613 --> 00:20:16.945
I'll still need, um...
help with the details.

00:20:17.049 --> 00:20:18.812
Put together a team.

00:20:18.884 --> 00:20:21.318
Use whatever
resources you need.

00:20:23.956 --> 00:20:27.483
A power ratio

00:20:27.559 --> 00:20:30.926
of approximately
60 terawatts

00:20:30.996 --> 00:20:32.224
should do the trick.

00:20:32.297 --> 00:20:33.229
You think that's enough?

00:20:33.298 --> 00:20:36.665
Should be, but then,
we have to compensate

00:20:36.735 --> 00:20:38.134
for gravimetric interference.

00:20:38.203 --> 00:20:39.534
And how do we do that?

00:20:39.605 --> 00:20:40.833
I was thinking...

00:20:40.906 --> 00:20:43.067
what if we applied
a narrowband filter

00:20:43.141 --> 00:20:44.733
to the transponder signal?

00:20:46.945 --> 00:20:47.969
Barclay strikes again.

00:20:48.113 --> 00:20:49.740
What's going on here?

00:20:49.815 --> 00:20:51.077
Commander...

00:20:51.149 --> 00:20:52.275
Who's your friend, Reg?

00:20:52.351 --> 00:20:54.342
Yes, aren't you going
to introduce me?

00:20:54.419 --> 00:20:55.909
Computer, delete characters.

00:20:57.489 --> 00:21:00.458
I thought I told you
to go home.

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:04.594
I was, uh... working.

00:21:04.663 --> 00:21:06.893
You call this work?

00:21:06.965 --> 00:21:12.301
You've created holograms
of the Voyager crew.

00:21:12.371 --> 00:21:15.033
Oh, it-it... it-it's
not what you think.

00:21:15.107 --> 00:21:18.167
It's an interactive,
uh, diagnostic program.

00:21:18.243 --> 00:21:21.235
I designed it to help
me... solve problems.

00:21:21.313 --> 00:21:23.713
How long have you been in here?

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:26.415
Since the briefing.

00:21:26.485 --> 00:21:28.419
The briefing ended
ten hours ago.

00:21:31.223 --> 00:21:34.522
I... I know
that I embarrassed you

00:21:34.593 --> 00:21:36.925
in front of the Admiral

00:21:36.995 --> 00:21:39.190
and I am... I'm sorry.

00:21:39.264 --> 00:21:40.959
I wanted to refine my idea,

00:21:41.033 --> 00:21:42.864
so that I could present you

00:21:42.934 --> 00:21:45.334
with a specific plan,
and I've done that, Pete.

00:21:45.404 --> 00:21:46.598
You were right

00:21:46.672 --> 00:21:48.606
about the wormhole idea
being too expansive.

00:21:48.674 --> 00:21:50.266
So, I've-I've scaled it back...

00:21:50.342 --> 00:21:53.573
All the extra time
you've been putting in...

00:21:53.645 --> 00:21:55.909
if I checked the holo-logs,

00:21:55.981 --> 00:21:58.541
would I find
you've been spending

00:21:58.617 --> 00:22:00.141
those hours in here?

00:22:00.218 --> 00:22:04.780
Well, not-not all that time.

00:22:04.856 --> 00:22:06.585
How much of it?

00:22:08.193 --> 00:22:09.922
Maybe, uh...

00:22:10.028 --> 00:22:11.620
20 or...

00:22:11.697 --> 00:22:13.927
30 hours a week.

00:22:14.066 --> 00:22:16.057
Don't you think
that's a little excessive?

00:22:16.134 --> 00:22:19.934
Uh, not if it helps us
contact Voyager.

00:22:22.541 --> 00:22:25.942
Before I brought you
onto my team...

00:22:26.044 --> 00:22:28.308
I reviewed your file.

00:22:28.380 --> 00:22:32.680
You've struggled
with holo-addiction before.

00:22:35.220 --> 00:22:36.482
From where I stand,

00:22:36.555 --> 00:22:39.080
it looks like
you've had a relapse.

00:22:39.157 --> 00:22:42.149
I-I know it-it may look
that way, but...

00:22:42.227 --> 00:22:43.455
I think you need counseling.

00:22:43.528 --> 00:22:45.120
What I need is

00:22:45.197 --> 00:22:47.859
for you to pay attention
to my ideas.

00:22:49.901 --> 00:22:54.395
I should've been paying more
attention to your behavior.

00:22:54.473 --> 00:22:56.839
I thought I was being a friend

00:22:56.908 --> 00:22:58.933
by giving you some leeway.

00:22:59.010 --> 00:23:00.875
I didn't realize how...

00:23:00.946 --> 00:23:03.813
involved you've
become with Voyager.

00:23:03.882 --> 00:23:05.474
Well, is it really so wrong?

00:23:05.550 --> 00:23:08.610
Do you have any idea
what it must be like for them

00:23:08.687 --> 00:23:10.814
to be stranded
60,000 light-years

00:23:10.889 --> 00:23:12.151
from home?

00:23:12.224 --> 00:23:17.059
Do you have any idea...
how lonely that must be?

00:23:17.129 --> 00:23:19.063
I'm sorry, Reg...

00:23:19.131 --> 00:23:23.693
but until you get some help,
you're off the project.

00:23:23.769 --> 00:23:25.828
You-you can't do that.

00:23:25.904 --> 00:23:28.429
You've given me no choice.

00:23:28.507 --> 00:23:30.941
This hologrid and the lab

00:23:31.042 --> 00:23:33.738
are officially off limits.

00:23:33.812 --> 00:23:36.474
Now, go home.

00:23:36.548 --> 00:23:37.947
I won't leave...

00:23:38.049 --> 00:23:40.745
not until you've heard
what I have to say.

00:23:40.819 --> 00:23:41.877
Reg!

00:23:44.489 --> 00:23:47.754
Don't make me call Security.

00:24:03.475 --> 00:24:04.806
What is it, Nicole?

00:24:04.876 --> 00:24:06.537
He's still here.

00:24:06.611 --> 00:24:09.079
You told him I have
a meeting scheduled at 1500?

00:24:09.147 --> 00:24:10.171
Yes, sir.

00:24:10.248 --> 00:24:11.374
He won't go away.

00:24:11.450 --> 00:24:14.214
Send him in.

00:24:14.286 --> 00:24:15.776
Yes, sir.

00:24:17.956 --> 00:24:20.857
Admiral, uh,
th-thank, thank you,

00:24:20.926 --> 00:24:22.154
uh, for seeing me.

00:24:22.227 --> 00:24:24.661
You're frightening
my secretary, Mr. Barclay.

00:24:24.729 --> 00:24:26.094
You have five minutes.

00:24:28.667 --> 00:24:30.897
Five minutes, right?

00:24:30.969 --> 00:24:32.197
Sit down.

00:24:34.272 --> 00:24:37.241
Uh, first... first,
I-I-I want to apologize

00:24:37.309 --> 00:24:39.834
for speaking out of turn
yesterday.

00:24:39.911 --> 00:24:41.242
L-it's only because I...

00:24:41.313 --> 00:24:43.406
I, I care so much
about Voyager.

00:24:43.482 --> 00:24:45.313
Yes, Commander Harkins
has informed me

00:24:45.383 --> 00:24:47.112
about your attachment
to the crew.

00:24:47.185 --> 00:24:49.176
I understand
you've been spending time

00:24:49.254 --> 00:24:52.155
with a holographic re-creation
of my son, among others.

00:24:52.224 --> 00:24:54.215
Frankly, I find that

00:24:54.292 --> 00:24:56.226
rather disturbing.

00:24:56.294 --> 00:24:59.127
Well, I understand
h-how you could see it that way,

00:24:59.197 --> 00:25:02.428
but, uh, that does not negate
the fact that I have a plan

00:25:02.501 --> 00:25:04.298
for communicating with Voyager.

00:25:04.369 --> 00:25:08.237
Commander Harkins doesn't seem
to think your plan is viable.

00:25:08.306 --> 00:25:10.570
I have refined the idea.

00:25:10.642 --> 00:25:12.109
I've simplified it.

00:25:12.177 --> 00:25:13.303
All I'm asking for

00:25:13.378 --> 00:25:14.902
is a chance to try.

00:25:15.046 --> 00:25:19.142
And if I'm right, it could mean
a chance to talk to Tom.

00:25:23.421 --> 00:25:27.357
In my opinion, Commander Harkins
removed you from the project

00:25:27.425 --> 00:25:30.223
with good cause,
and that's his prerogative.

00:25:30.295 --> 00:25:32.388
I won't let my personal feelings

00:25:32.464 --> 00:25:34.329
interfere
with Starfleet procedure.

00:25:38.103 --> 00:25:42.062
I... I've broken protocol
and I should be punished,

00:25:42.140 --> 00:25:44.870
but the crew
of the Voyager shouldn't be

00:25:44.943 --> 00:25:47.275
and neither...
neither should you.

00:25:47.345 --> 00:25:49.779
I just need access
to the lab

00:25:49.848 --> 00:25:51.509
for one more day.

00:25:51.583 --> 00:25:53.244
After that, if I...

00:25:53.318 --> 00:25:54.717
uh, if I'm wrong,

00:25:54.786 --> 00:25:57.482
I'll resign my commission.

00:26:00.659 --> 00:26:02.684
I'll order a review
of your findings.

00:26:02.761 --> 00:26:04.888
If it's concluded
your ideas are valid,

00:26:04.963 --> 00:26:07.363
I'll instruct Commander Harkins
to pursue it.

00:26:07.432 --> 00:26:09.024
But... I'm
the one who knows...

00:26:09.100 --> 00:26:11.694
That's the best
I can do, Mr. Barclay.

00:26:11.770 --> 00:26:13.237
Good day.

00:26:18.677 --> 00:26:21.578
So the meeting went well.

00:26:21.646 --> 00:26:24.308
No, no, no.
It didn't, not at all.

00:26:24.382 --> 00:26:25.781
The Admiral said

00:26:25.850 --> 00:26:27.750
he'd review your findings.

00:26:27.819 --> 00:26:28.843
Don't you see?

00:26:28.920 --> 00:26:30.717
He was just trying
to get rid of me

00:26:30.789 --> 00:26:31.881
just like Harkins.

00:26:31.957 --> 00:26:33.151
Try to relax.

00:26:33.224 --> 00:26:36.125
Now you understand
why I need your help.

00:26:36.194 --> 00:26:37.923
Yes, I do.

00:26:38.063 --> 00:26:40.190
You-you have to call the Admiral

00:26:40.265 --> 00:26:42.927
in your official capacity
as a Starfleet Counselor

00:26:43.068 --> 00:26:45.127
and tell him that
I am psychologically fit

00:26:45.203 --> 00:26:46.227
to return to work.

00:26:49.541 --> 00:26:50.940
I can't do that.

00:26:51.076 --> 00:26:53.636
Why not?!

00:26:53.712 --> 00:26:54.940
Look at yourself.

00:26:55.013 --> 00:26:57.811
You're experiencing
acute anxiety,

00:26:57.882 --> 00:26:59.144
sleeplessness,

00:26:59.217 --> 00:27:00.275
paranoia.

00:27:00.352 --> 00:27:01.842
You did what you could.

00:27:01.920 --> 00:27:06.084
Now it's time to let Starfleet
worry about Voyager.

00:27:06.157 --> 00:27:08.455
We need to take care of you.

00:27:08.526 --> 00:27:11.256
There is nothing
wrong with me!

00:27:11.329 --> 00:27:14.025
You said yourself, you've become

00:27:14.099 --> 00:27:15.896
obsessed with Voyager.

00:27:16.001 --> 00:27:17.400
What if I have?

00:27:17.469 --> 00:27:20.199
If an obsession helps me
to do my job better,

00:27:20.271 --> 00:27:22.637
i-it's a sacrifice
I am willing to make.

00:27:22.707 --> 00:27:25.574
A little instability
in exchange for contact

00:27:25.644 --> 00:27:27.908
with a stranded starship.

00:27:28.046 --> 00:27:29.445
Isn't Voyager
more important

00:27:29.514 --> 00:27:31.175
than my
psychological condition?

00:27:31.249 --> 00:27:35.117
Voyager is important,
but so are you.

00:27:35.186 --> 00:27:37.051
That ship...

00:27:43.294 --> 00:27:45.262
that crew...

00:27:48.533 --> 00:27:50.899
they're all I have.

00:27:56.741 --> 00:27:58.936
Tell me why that is.

00:27:59.077 --> 00:28:03.878
Ever... ever since
I-I left the Enterprise,

00:28:03.982 --> 00:28:07.884
things haven't...
haven't been the same.

00:28:08.019 --> 00:28:11.079
It's as if...

00:28:15.193 --> 00:28:17.354
I lost my family.

00:28:17.429 --> 00:28:22.992
So you created a new family
on the holodeck.

00:28:23.068 --> 00:28:25.593
Only they're not real.

00:28:25.670 --> 00:28:29.299
I didn't know how else...

00:28:29.374 --> 00:28:31.308
how else to cope.

00:28:34.345 --> 00:28:37.678
Do you remember when you first
came aboard the Enterprise?

00:28:37.749 --> 00:28:40.445
You had trouble
fitting in, didn't you?

00:28:40.518 --> 00:28:46.548
But after a while, you
started to make friends.

00:28:46.624 --> 00:28:49.752
You can learn to do
the same thing here on Earth.

00:28:49.828 --> 00:28:53.355
Oh, I... I don't know how.

00:28:53.431 --> 00:28:55.797
We'll work on it together.

00:28:57.669 --> 00:29:00.467
You're, you're scheduled
to depart tomorrow.

00:29:00.538 --> 00:29:03.200
I've decided
to ask Captain Picard

00:29:03.274 --> 00:29:05.868
for a temporary
leave of absence...

00:29:05.977 --> 00:29:09.879
to spend some time
with an old friend.

00:29:09.948 --> 00:29:11.745
Oh, Deanna, you...
you-you, you don't,

00:29:11.816 --> 00:29:13.113
you don't have to do that.

00:29:13.184 --> 00:29:16.381
Try and stop me.

00:29:33.471 --> 00:29:34.733
I'm sorry, Neelix.

00:29:34.806 --> 00:29:36.034
I have to leave.

00:29:37.642 --> 00:29:40.270
No, no,
you can't talk me out of it.

00:29:50.021 --> 00:29:52.353
Authorization code required.

00:29:52.423 --> 00:29:54.050
Barclay-alpha-one-seven-gamma.

00:29:54.125 --> 00:29:55.387
Access denied.

00:29:55.460 --> 00:29:57.792
That code
has been de-authorized.

00:30:12.310 --> 00:30:14.642
Computer, reenter

00:30:14.712 --> 00:30:17.943
authorization code
Barclay-alpha-one-seven-gamma.

00:30:19.851 --> 00:30:21.614
Access authorized.

00:30:41.773 --> 00:30:44.936
Computer, interface
with the MIDAS Array.

00:30:55.820 --> 00:30:59.119
Activate the control matrix.

00:31:05.296 --> 00:31:06.820
Matrix activated.

00:31:06.898 --> 00:31:09.162
Full power
to the graviton emitters.

00:31:09.234 --> 00:31:11.668
Emitters powering.

00:31:11.736 --> 00:31:14.170
Scan the area
surrounding the Array

00:31:14.239 --> 00:31:16.503
for a class-B itinerant pulsar.

00:31:16.574 --> 00:31:20.840
A pulsar has been detected
at coordinates 227 by 41 mark 6.

00:31:20.912 --> 00:31:22.846
Good, good.

00:31:22.914 --> 00:31:28.511
Direct a 60 terawatt
tachyon beam toward the pulsar.

00:31:28.586 --> 00:31:30.850
Tachyon beam initiated.

00:31:30.922 --> 00:31:34.949
How long
until levels are sufficient

00:31:35.026 --> 00:31:41.522
to produce a gravimetric surge
of five million teradynes?

00:31:41.599 --> 00:31:44.534
Approximately 17 minutes.

00:31:47.605 --> 00:31:51.871
Computer, is there
a micro-wormhole present

00:31:51.943 --> 00:31:54.468
at coordinates 343 by 27?

00:31:54.545 --> 00:31:56.012
Scanning.

00:31:58.383 --> 00:31:59.816
Affirmative.

00:31:59.884 --> 00:32:02.148
I knew it.

00:32:02.220 --> 00:32:04.484
Adjust the phase alignment

00:32:04.555 --> 00:32:07.149
to direct
the wormhole's trajectory

00:32:07.225 --> 00:32:11.491
to Delta Quadrant, Grid 9,
Sector 41751.

00:32:11.562 --> 00:32:14.156
Trajectory established.

00:32:14.232 --> 00:32:17.326
Open Starfleet Emergency Channel

00:32:17.402 --> 00:32:20.860
and transmit
toward the singularity.

00:32:22.073 --> 00:32:23.938
Channel open.

00:32:24.075 --> 00:32:26.509
Starfleet Command
to USS Voyager.

00:32:26.577 --> 00:32:28.044
Come in, Voyager.

00:32:29.914 --> 00:32:33.509
Voyager, do you hear me?

00:32:33.584 --> 00:32:36.985
This is
Lieutenant Reginald Barclay.

00:32:38.022 --> 00:32:41.253
Step away from the controls.

00:32:41.326 --> 00:32:43.191
Pete.

00:32:43.261 --> 00:32:45.229
I... I've sent a message.

00:32:47.098 --> 00:32:49.498
Stand down, Mr. Barclay.

00:32:51.536 --> 00:32:53.003
All right.

00:32:56.207 --> 00:32:57.936
You win.

00:32:58.009 --> 00:32:59.476
Computer...

00:32:59.544 --> 00:33:01.341
transfer controls
to hologrid

00:33:01.412 --> 00:33:02.902
program Barclay pi-three

00:33:03.047 --> 00:33:04.514
and restrict access!

00:33:04.582 --> 00:33:05.844
Stop him.

00:33:05.917 --> 00:33:07.748
Stun him if you have to.

00:33:22.567 --> 00:33:24.262
Tuvok, did you
see those two men?

00:33:24.335 --> 00:33:25.495
I did not.

00:33:25.570 --> 00:33:26.867
Well, they look like
Starfleet Security,

00:33:26.938 --> 00:33:27.905
but they're not.

00:33:27.972 --> 00:33:28.904
Intruders?

00:33:28.973 --> 00:33:30.497
They're after me.
I need your help.

00:33:30.575 --> 00:33:31.837
Tuvok to all hands.

00:33:31.909 --> 00:33:33.171
Intruder alert.

00:33:33.244 --> 00:33:35.838
Computer, locate
any unauthorized personnel

00:33:35.913 --> 00:33:37.505
aboard Voyager.

00:33:37.582 --> 00:33:40.847
Two unidentified humans,
Deck 4, Section 8.

00:33:40.918 --> 00:33:43.045
Isolate them
with force fields.

00:33:48.426 --> 00:33:50.189
Security to Commander Harkins.

00:33:50.261 --> 00:33:52.593
We've been isolated
by force fields.

00:33:52.663 --> 00:33:54.460
Can you shut down the program?

00:33:54.532 --> 00:33:55.999
I'm working on it.

00:33:57.368 --> 00:33:58.801
Access denied.

00:33:58.870 --> 00:34:01.464
Hologrid controls
have been encrypted.

00:34:01.539 --> 00:34:03.166
Harkins to Security.

00:34:03.241 --> 00:34:05.175
I need reinforcements.

00:34:06.244 --> 00:34:08.007
Computer, redirect
the wormhole's trajectory

00:34:08.079 --> 00:34:10.604
to Delta Quadrant, Grid 11,
Sector 64238,

00:34:10.681 --> 00:34:12.478
and retransmit the message.

00:34:12.550 --> 00:34:14.484
Trajectory established.
Transmitting.

00:34:14.552 --> 00:34:15.484
A wormhole?

00:34:15.553 --> 00:34:16.645
What's going on?

00:34:16.721 --> 00:34:18.416
I'm just trying
to help some friends.

00:34:18.489 --> 00:34:19.421
Is there a response?

00:34:19.490 --> 00:34:20.582
Negative.

00:34:20.658 --> 00:34:22.250
Computer, redirect
the wormhole's trajectory.

00:34:22.326 --> 00:34:23.293
Reg!

00:34:24.562 --> 00:34:26.086
You'll have to
come with me, sir.

00:34:26.164 --> 00:34:28.530
I'll cover for you.

00:34:38.009 --> 00:34:41.445
Computer,
seal Jefferies Tube Door J53.

00:34:43.681 --> 00:34:46.047
Computer, cut all power
to the hologrid.

00:34:46.117 --> 00:34:47.550
Unable to comply.

00:34:47.618 --> 00:34:50.314
Main power controls
have been encrypted.

00:34:50.388 --> 00:34:52.151
Very clever, Reg.

00:34:52.223 --> 00:34:54.316
Security to Commander Harkins.

00:34:54.392 --> 00:34:55.825
We've lost him, sir.

00:34:55.893 --> 00:34:57.588
I've got an idea.

00:34:57.662 --> 00:34:59.129
I'm coming in.

00:35:03.401 --> 00:35:04.493
I know you.

00:35:04.569 --> 00:35:05.831
You're Reg's friend.

00:35:05.903 --> 00:35:07.200
You've got something to do

00:35:07.271 --> 00:35:09.102
with what's going on here,
don't you?

00:35:09.173 --> 00:35:11.266
Computer, disengage
primary coolant system.

00:35:11.342 --> 00:35:13.105
Are you crazy? That'll cause

00:35:13.177 --> 00:35:15.145
a warp core breach!

00:35:15.213 --> 00:35:16.578
Exactly.

00:35:20.084 --> 00:35:22.211
Mr. Barclay,
I want an explanation

00:35:22.286 --> 00:35:24.516
for what's going on
aboard my ship.

00:35:24.589 --> 00:35:26.750
I'm looking after Voyager's
best interests, Captain.

00:35:26.824 --> 00:35:28.519
You're just going to have
to trust me on that.

00:35:28.593 --> 00:35:31.756
You've never given me
any reason to doubt you before.

00:35:31.829 --> 00:35:34.457
Computer, redirect
the wormhole's trajectory

00:35:34.532 --> 00:35:36.830
to Delta Quadrant,
Grid 10, Sector 3658

00:35:36.901 --> 00:35:38.528
and retransmit the message.

00:35:38.603 --> 00:35:43.370
Trajectory established.
Transmitting.

00:35:43.441 --> 00:35:44.874
Who are you trying
to contact, Reg?

00:35:44.942 --> 00:35:47.877
Warning.
Warp core breach in 45 seconds.

00:35:47.945 --> 00:35:50.641
Bridge to Engineering. Report.

00:35:50.715 --> 00:35:52.148
Shut down the program, Reg.

00:35:52.216 --> 00:35:53.444
Janeway to Security.

00:35:53.518 --> 00:35:55.281
Intruders on the Bridge.

00:35:55.353 --> 00:35:56.752
Computer,
establish a force field

00:35:56.821 --> 00:35:57.947
around the science station.

00:35:58.055 --> 00:35:59.784
Warning.
Warp core breach in 30 seconds.

00:35:59.857 --> 00:36:01.188
Harry, get down
to Engineering.

00:36:01.259 --> 00:36:02.851
Seal that breach.

00:36:02.927 --> 00:36:05.122
Force fields aren't going
to help you, Reg. It's over.

00:36:05.196 --> 00:36:07.630
But this is my last chance.

00:36:07.698 --> 00:36:09.495
Warp core breach in 20 seconds.

00:36:09.567 --> 00:36:12.627
Captain to all hands.
Abandon ship.

00:36:17.241 --> 00:36:20.335
Warp core breach in ten seconds.

00:36:20.411 --> 00:36:23.539
One way or another,
this program's going to end.

00:36:23.614 --> 00:36:26.811
...seven, six...

00:36:26.884 --> 00:36:28.146
Good-bye, Captain.

00:36:28.219 --> 00:36:29.311
...four...

00:36:29.387 --> 00:36:31.252
Computer, end program.

00:36:31.322 --> 00:36:32.721
...two...

00:36:50.541 --> 00:36:52.805
I'm ready for my lesson.

00:36:52.877 --> 00:36:55.072
I've concluded that
teaching you to sing

00:36:55.146 --> 00:36:56.943
is an inefficient
use of my time.

00:36:57.048 --> 00:37:00.313
But I... I've...
I've been practicing.

00:37:00.384 --> 00:37:02.875
In your case,
practice is irrelevant.

00:37:02.987 --> 00:37:05.080
Your vocal chords
are incapable

00:37:05.156 --> 00:37:07.488
of producing
basic diatonic tones,

00:37:07.558 --> 00:37:10.493
not to mention your
rhythmic shortcomings.

00:37:10.561 --> 00:37:13.325
I sound so good
in the sonic shower.

00:37:13.397 --> 00:37:15.160
Perhaps you should
confine your efforts

00:37:15.233 --> 00:37:16.530
to that location.

00:37:23.140 --> 00:37:25.108
Astrometrics to the Bridge.

00:37:25.176 --> 00:37:26.837
Go ahead, Seven.

00:37:26.911 --> 00:37:29.607
I've detected what appears
to be a micro-wormhole

00:37:29.680 --> 00:37:33.207
at coordinates 194.6 by 35.

00:37:33.284 --> 00:37:35.115
A micro-wormhole?

00:37:35.186 --> 00:37:37.620
I believe a message is being
transmitted through it...

00:37:40.591 --> 00:37:43.321
on a Starfleet
Emergency Channel.

00:37:51.636 --> 00:37:53.365
Let's hear it, Harry.

00:37:53.437 --> 00:37:56.235
Starfleet Command
to USS Voyager.

00:37:58.042 --> 00:38:01.170
Try applying a narrowband filter
to the signal processor.

00:38:02.880 --> 00:38:04.313
Do you hear me?

00:38:04.382 --> 00:38:10.218
This is
Lieutenant Reginald Barclay.

00:38:10.288 --> 00:38:11.721
That's it.

00:38:11.789 --> 00:38:13.279
Whoever this Barclay is,

00:38:13.357 --> 00:38:15.086
he stopped transmitting.

00:38:15.159 --> 00:38:17.821
The micro-wormhole is collapsing

00:38:17.895 --> 00:38:19.760
at a rate of.2 percent
per second.

00:38:19.830 --> 00:38:22.060
That doesn't give us much time.

00:38:22.133 --> 00:38:23.395
To do what?

00:38:23.467 --> 00:38:25.059
To send a message
back through

00:38:25.136 --> 00:38:27.104
and hope Mr. Barclay
is listening.

00:38:30.241 --> 00:38:31.299
It should have worked.

00:38:31.375 --> 00:38:33.070
I don't understand
why it didn't.

00:38:34.578 --> 00:38:36.045
There you are.

00:38:36.113 --> 00:38:37.910
I've reviewed
Mr. Barclay's plan.

00:38:38.049 --> 00:38:39.914
I think it's
worth an attempt.

00:38:39.984 --> 00:38:42.748
He's already tried, sir,
without your authorization.

00:38:42.820 --> 00:38:44.253
It didn't work.

00:38:44.322 --> 00:38:46.483
I'm sorry to hear that.

00:38:46.557 --> 00:38:47.649
So am I, sir.

00:38:47.725 --> 00:38:49.488
I appreciate
your confidence in me,

00:38:49.560 --> 00:38:51.118
but I... I don't deserve it.

00:38:51.195 --> 00:38:53.561
What would you like me
to do with him, Admiral?

00:38:53.631 --> 00:38:56.031
He broke into the lab,
accessed the MIDAS Array,

00:38:56.100 --> 00:38:57.533
resisted arrest.

00:38:57.601 --> 00:39:00.331
You've put me
in a difficult position, son.

00:39:00.404 --> 00:39:02.736
I was hoping
that we'd be able to...

00:39:04.175 --> 00:39:05.574
We're receiving

00:39:05.643 --> 00:39:06.871
a transmission.

00:39:07.011 --> 00:39:07.875
From where?

00:39:08.012 --> 00:39:09.502
Coordinates 343.6

00:39:09.580 --> 00:39:10.842
by 27.

00:39:10.915 --> 00:39:12.177
The wormhole.

00:39:12.249 --> 00:39:14.479
Starfleet Command, come in.

00:39:14.552 --> 00:39:16.884
Voyager.

00:39:16.987 --> 00:39:20.320
Reg, give me a hand
clearing up the signal.

00:39:22.193 --> 00:39:24.889
Lower the filter band
by.3 kilohertz.

00:39:24.962 --> 00:39:26.896
This is Captain Kathryn Janeway.

00:39:26.964 --> 00:39:28.397
Do you read me?

00:39:28.466 --> 00:39:31.060
I think she's talking to you.

00:39:31.135 --> 00:39:32.659
Captain...

00:39:32.737 --> 00:39:36.901
this is
Lieutenant Reginald Barclay

00:39:36.974 --> 00:39:39.568
at Starfleet Command.

00:39:39.643 --> 00:39:42.407
It's good to hear
your voice, Lieutenant.

00:39:42.480 --> 00:39:44.471
We've been waiting a long time

00:39:44.548 --> 00:39:46.175
for this moment.

00:39:46.250 --> 00:39:47.740
The feeling is mutual.

00:39:47.818 --> 00:39:49.843
Unfortunately, the
micro-wormhole is collapsing.

00:39:49.920 --> 00:39:51.512
We have only a few moments.

00:39:51.589 --> 00:39:52.920
Understood.

00:39:53.023 --> 00:39:56.015
We are transmitting
our ship's logs, crew reports,

00:39:56.093 --> 00:39:58.357
and navigational records
to you now.

00:39:58.429 --> 00:40:00.522
Acknowledged,
and we're sending you

00:40:00.598 --> 00:40:03.624
data on some new
hyper-subspace technology.

00:40:03.701 --> 00:40:05.430
We're hoping, eventually,
to use it

00:40:05.503 --> 00:40:07.767
to keep in regular contact,
and we're including some

00:40:07.838 --> 00:40:10.272
recommended modifications
for your com system.

00:40:10.341 --> 00:40:12.707
We'll implement them
as soon as possible.

00:40:12.777 --> 00:40:14.836
Uh, there's someone else here

00:40:14.912 --> 00:40:17.972
who would also
like to say something.

00:40:19.850 --> 00:40:21.681
This is Admiral Paris.

00:40:21.752 --> 00:40:23.185
Hello, sir.

00:40:23.254 --> 00:40:24.949
How are your people holding up?

00:40:25.055 --> 00:40:26.454
Very well.

00:40:26.524 --> 00:40:29.618
They're an exemplary crew,

00:40:29.693 --> 00:40:31.661
your son included.

00:40:32.730 --> 00:40:36.359
Tell him... tell him I miss him,

00:40:36.434 --> 00:40:39.232
and I'm proud of him.

00:40:39.303 --> 00:40:42.329
He heard you, Admiral.

00:40:42.406 --> 00:40:43.839
The wormhole is collapsing.

00:40:43.908 --> 00:40:46.138
I want you all to know
we're doing everything we can

00:40:46.210 --> 00:40:47.177
to bring you home.

00:40:47.244 --> 00:40:49.178
We appreciate it, sir.

00:40:49.246 --> 00:40:51.373
Keep a docking bay open for us.

00:40:51.449 --> 00:40:52.746
We hope to...

00:40:54.485 --> 00:40:57.454
That's it. They're gone.

00:40:58.989 --> 00:41:00.820
You did it, Reg.

00:41:00.891 --> 00:41:03.257
I'm sorry I doubted you.

00:41:06.430 --> 00:41:08.728
Why the long face, Mr. Barclay?

00:41:08.799 --> 00:41:14.101
Because...
because it's over, sir.

00:41:14.171 --> 00:41:17.436
No, Lieutenant.

00:41:17.508 --> 00:41:21.604
I'd say that Project Voyager
is just beginning...

00:41:21.679 --> 00:41:23.271
thanks to you.

00:41:35.025 --> 00:41:36.959
Anyone know this Barclay?

00:41:37.027 --> 00:41:38.289
I took the liberty

00:41:38.362 --> 00:41:40.125
of reviewing
his personnel file.

00:41:40.197 --> 00:41:41.960
He's had a rather
colorful career,

00:41:42.099 --> 00:41:44.431
not to mention an
unusual medical history.

00:41:44.502 --> 00:41:46.766
He's recovered
from a variety of maladies

00:41:46.837 --> 00:41:48.395
including transporter phobia

00:41:48.472 --> 00:41:49.734
and holo-addiction.

00:41:49.807 --> 00:41:50.899
Well, whatever his problems,

00:41:50.975 --> 00:41:52.567
he certainly came through
for us.

00:41:52.643 --> 00:41:54.577
Starfleet should
give him a promotion.

00:41:54.645 --> 00:41:56.078
I've finished
analyzing the data

00:41:56.146 --> 00:41:57.306
Mr. Barclay sent.

00:41:57.381 --> 00:41:59.372
The hyper-subspace
technology is promising.

00:41:59.450 --> 00:42:00.815
I believe
we can look forward

00:42:00.885 --> 00:42:02.580
to future communications
with Earth.

00:42:02.653 --> 00:42:04.086
Well, that calls for a toast.

00:42:04.154 --> 00:42:05.985
Care to do the honors, Tom?

00:42:08.492 --> 00:42:11.620
To... my dad.

00:42:11.695 --> 00:42:13.060
It's nice to know

00:42:13.130 --> 00:42:14.597
he's still there.

00:42:14.665 --> 00:42:16.929
And to the newest
honorary member

00:42:17.001 --> 00:42:18.332
of the Voyager crew,

00:42:18.402 --> 00:42:20.802
Reginald Barclay,
whoever you are.

00:42:20.871 --> 00:42:22.133
Hear, hear.

00:42:22.206 --> 00:42:23.673
To Mr. Barclay.

00:42:23.741 --> 00:42:25.641
Congratulations.

00:42:25.709 --> 00:42:29.110
Well, I'm not... not sure
I deserve congratulations.

00:42:29.179 --> 00:42:30.441
Why not?

00:42:30.514 --> 00:42:31.947
It's quite an accomplishment.

00:42:32.016 --> 00:42:33.847
I, I couldn't have done it
without your help.

00:42:33.918 --> 00:42:35.943
Why did Commander Harkins
have to say about it?

00:42:36.020 --> 00:42:38.580
Well, I think...
I think he was pleased.

00:42:38.656 --> 00:42:39.816
Why wouldn't he be?

00:42:39.890 --> 00:42:41.187
You're quite a catch.

00:42:41.258 --> 00:42:43.852
Well, not everyone
would want his sister-in-law

00:42:43.928 --> 00:42:45.759
to date someone with my history.

00:42:45.829 --> 00:42:48.229
It's a new era.

00:42:48.299 --> 00:42:51.234
So, tell me
all about the lucky lady.

00:42:51.302 --> 00:42:52.701
I want details.

00:42:52.770 --> 00:42:56.968
Well, her name is Hope.

00:42:57.041 --> 00:42:58.133
You're kidding.

00:42:58.208 --> 00:43:00.267
No, and-and-and...

00:43:00.344 --> 00:43:02.642
she loves cats.
